     5177 :: 9.45 A.M. Fort Monroe July 10, 1863 . Gen Halleck Gordon's division and four batteries of artillery are Embarking at Yorktown and two regiments of Infantry at Norfolk two more brigades will embark as soon as I have transportation I expect steamers back today I have no transports for army wagons signed Jno. A. Dix weather very warm 12 M. Fort Monroe July 10, 1863 Gen Halleck In my dispatch this morning I mentioned that I had no transports for army
